---
import CompareLayout from '../../layouts/CompareLayout.astro'

const models = [
  { name: 'Claude Sonnet 4.5', correctnessBefore: '3/5', correctnessAfter: '5/5' },
  { name: 'Claude Haiku 4.5', correctnessBefore: '2/5', correctnessAfter: '5/5' },
  { name: 'GPT-4o', correctnessBefore: '0/5', correctnessAfter: '5/5' },
  { name: 'GPT-4o-mini', correctnessBefore: '1/5', correctnessAfter: '5/5' },
]

const stats = [
  { value: '4', label: 'Leading LLMs tested', sub: 'Claude and GPT families', tone: '' },
  { value: '100%', label: 'Hallucinated on clean PRs', sub: 'Every model, every time', tone: 'ui-c-crit' },
  { value: '0%', label: 'Hallucinations with Buoy', sub: 'Scanner-verified output', tone: 'ui-c-ok' },
  { value: '5/5', label: 'Correctness with Buoy', sub: 'Across all 4 models', tone: 'ui-c-ok' },
]

const llmIssues = [
  { sev: 'critical', word: 'Error', file: 'Card.tsx', line: 'line 112', note: 'file is 61 lines', text: 'Hardcoded color', value: '#f9fafb', fix: 'Use a design token instead' },
  { sev: 'critical', word: 'Error', file: 'Card.tsx', line: 'line 34', note: '', text: 'Hardcoded spacing', value: '16px', fix: 'Replace with var(--spacing-md)' },
  { sev: 'warning', word: 'Warn', file: 'Badge.tsx', line: 'line 7', note: '', text: 'Non-standard border radius', value: '6px', fix: 'Should use var(--radius-sm)' },
]
---

<CompareLayout
  title="LLM Code Review Hallucinations | Why Buoy Uses Deterministic Scanning"
  description="We tested 4 leading LLMs reviewing clean PRs. Every one hallucinated design system issues that didn't exist. Buoy's deterministic scanner eliminates false positives."
  keywords="llm code review, ai hallucination, design system review, deterministic scanning, buoy vs ai review"
  heroTitle="Your design system deserves facts, not hallucinations."
  heroDescription="We tested every major AI code reviewer on a clean PR with zero design system issues. Every single one invented problems that didn't exist."
  competitor="LLM Code Review"
>
  <div slot="hero" class="ui-tray"><div class="ui-panel">
    <div class="ui-panel-head">Card.tsx, a clean 61-line file</div>
    <pre class="hf-code"><code>background: <span class="ui-token">var(--color-gray-50)</span>;</code></pre>
    <dl class="hf-rows">
      <div><dt class="ui-c-crit">LLM only</dt><dd><span class="ui-sev ui-sev-critical">Error</span> Hardcoded color <span class="ui-old">#f9fafb</span> at line 112 <span class="hf-them">(the file is 61 lines)</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ui-c-ok">Buoy</dt><dd><span class="ui-c-ok">No design system issues found.</span> <span class="hf-them">0 false positives.</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div></div>

  <section id="results" class="ui-section">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head"><h2>Same PR. Same code. Very different reviews.</h2><p>Four leading LLMs reviewed a clean PR using <code class="ui-token">var(--color-gray-50)</code> correctly. Zero real issues.</p></div>
      <div class="llm-stats">
        {stats.map((s) => (
          <div class="llm-stat">
            <p class={`llm-num ui-tnum ${s.tone}`}>{s.value}</p>
            <p class="llm-label">{s.label}</p>
            <p class="ui-note">{s.sub}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-section ui-section--band">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head">
        <h2>How Buoy eliminates hallucinations</h2>
        <p>The LLM never decides what's wrong. It only explains what the scanner already found.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="ui-steps">
        <li><span class="ui-step-n">1</span><div><h3>Scanner finds real issues <span class="ui-c-ok llm-tag">100% deterministic</span></h3><p>Deterministic analysis. Exact file, exact line, exact value. No guessing, no probability.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="ui-step-n">2</span><div><h3>LLM explains findings <span class="ui-c-lavender llm-tag">Constrained by facts</span></h3><p>The AI gets scanner output as context, not raw diffs. It explains why each issue matters and how to fix it.</p></div></li>
        <li><span class="ui-step-n">3</span><div><h3>Developer gets one-click fixes <span class="ui-c-buoy llm-tag">Verified replacements</span></h3><p>Every suggestion is verified against your actual token definitions. Copy, paste, done.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="ui-card ui-card--pad">
        <h3 class="llm-h3">The key insight</h3>
        <p>LLMs are great at explaining code. They're terrible at auditing it. Buoy uses each for what it's good at: the scanner audits, the LLM explains. The result is zero hallucinations and clear, actionable feedback.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-section">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head">
        <h2>Why do LLMs invent issues on clean code?</h2>
        <p>It's not a bug. It's how they work.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="ui-table ui-table--stack mt-8">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Task-completion bias</th><td>When you ask an LLM to "review this PR for design system issues," it wants to be helpful. If the code is clean, it will find something anyway, because saying "nothing's wrong" doesn't feel like completing the task.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Pattern hallucination</th><td>LLMs have seen millions of code reviews that found issues. They're pattern-matching against that history. A diff that "looks like" it might have a hardcoded color? The model will confidently assert it does.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">No source of truth</th><td>An LLM reviewing a diff doesn't know your token definitions. It doesn't know that <code class="ui-token">var(--color-gray-50)</code> is valid in your system. It's guessing based on the diff alone.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Line number fabrication</th><td>LLMs generate text sequentially. Line numbers are just tokens to them, not verified positions. That's how one model referenced "line 112" in a 61-line file.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-section ui-section--band">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head">
        <h2>Model-by-model results</h2>
        <p>Correctness scores reviewing the same clean PR, before and after Buoy's scanner is the source of truth.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="ui-table cmp-table mt-10">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">LLM only</th><th scope="col" class="cmp-buoy">With Buoy</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {models.map((m) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{m.name}</th>
              <td class="cmp-them"><span class={`llm-score ui-tnum ${m.correctnessBefore === '0/5' || m.correctnessBefore === '1/5' ? 'ui-c-crit' : 'ui-c-warn'}`}>{m.correctnessBefore}</span></td>
              <td class="cmp-buoy"><span class="llm-score ui-tnum ui-c-ok">{m.correctnessAfter}</span></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="ui-note mt-4">Every model <span class="ui-c-crit">hallucinated</span> issues on its own. With Buoy's scanner as the source of truth, <span class="ui-c-ok">none did</span>.</p>
      <p class="ui-after mt-8"><strong>GPT-4o scored 0/5 without Buoy.</strong> It claimed hex values like <code class="ui-old">#f9fafb</code> existed at specific lines when the actual code used <code class="ui-token">var(--color-gray-50)</code>. With Buoy as the source of truth, it scored 5/5.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ui-section">
    <div class="ui-wrap">
      <div class="ui-head">
        <h2>We're not anti-AI. We use AI.</h2>
        <p>Buoy's optional AI layer uses Claude to generate natural-language explanations and context-aware suggestions. The difference is that our AI is constrained by deterministic scanner output.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="ui-table ui-table--stack mt-8">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="ui-c-crit">LLM-only</th><td>Give the model a diff and hope for the best</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="ui-c-ok">Buoy</th><td>Scanner finds facts, AI explains them clearly</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="ui-after mt-8">Stop reviewing hallucinated issues. Buoy is free, open source, and runs in under a minute: <code class="ui-code">npx ahoybuoy dock</code></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</CompareLayout>

<style>
  .llm-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 380px), 1fr)); gap: 20px; }
  .llm-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; }
  .llm-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-weight: 600; }
  .llm-bot { color: var(--color-muted); font-weight: 400; font-size: 12px; }
  .llm-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .llm-list > li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 56px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); font-size: 14px; }
  .llm-list p { margin: 0; }
  .llm-loc { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .llm-text { color: var(--color-ink); margin-top: 2px !important; }
  .llm-fix { color: var(--color-muted); }
  .llm-foot { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; padding: 12px 18px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-muted); background: var(--color-raised); margin-top: auto; }
  .llm-clean { flex: 1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center; text-align: center; padding: 40px 24px; min-height: 220px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--color-muted); }
  .llm-clean p { margin: 0; max-width: 300px; }
  .llm-clean-h { font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px !important; }
  .llm-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-strong); }
  .llm-stat { padding: 24px 24px 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .llm-stat:first-child { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; }
  .llm-stat p { margin: 0; }
  .llm-num { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 44px; line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .llm-label { margin-top: 8px !important; color: var(--color-ink); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; }
  .llm-score { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; }
  .llm-tag { margin-left: 8px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; }
  .llm-h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: var(--text-h3); color: var(--color-ink); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .llm-stats { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .llm-stat { padding: 20px 16px 16px; border-left: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
    .llm-stat:nth-child(odd) { padding-left: 0; }
    .llm-tag { display: block; margin: 2px 0 0; }
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .hf-code { margin: 0; padding: 18px 20px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; background: var(--color-term); color: var(--color-body); }
  .hf-rows { margin: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line); }
  .hf-rows > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 96px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 12px; padding: 13px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .hf-rows > div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .hf-rows dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .hf-rows dd { margin: 0; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .hf-rows .hf-them { color: var(--color-muted); }
</style>
